//! Event System for World Factory
//! 
//! Defines historical events, event types, and event effects.
//! Events are the primary mechanism for history generation and timeline construction.
//!
//! ## Event Lifecycle
//! 
//! 1. **Creation** — Event generated by a system (settlement, war, discovery, etc.)
//! 2. **Application** — Event effects applied to world state (population change, border shift, etc.)
//! 3. **Timeline Insertion** — Event inserted into chronological timeline
//! 4. **Consequence Triggering** — Secondary events may be triggered by consequences
//!
//! ## EventType Categories
//! 
//! | Category | Types | Description |
//! |----------|-------|-------------|
//! | Political | Founding, Treaty, Reform, Succession, Alliance | Governance and diplomacy |
//! | Military | War, Battle, Siege, Conquest, Raid | Armed conflict events |
//! | Natural | Plague, Famine, Earthquake, Flood, Drought, Volcano | Environmental disasters |
//! | Cultural | Festival, Art, Invention, Migration, Immigration | Social and cultural shifts |
//! | Discovery | Exploration, Discovery, FirstContact, Invention | Knowledge advancement |
//! | Catastrophe | Collapse, Destruction, Extinction, MeteorStrike | Major disruptive events |
//!
//! ## Usage Example
//! 
//! ```rust
//! use world_factory::events::{Event, EventBuilder, HistoricalTime, EventEffect};
//! 
//! let event = EventBuilder::new("The Great Plague")
//!     .event_type(EventType::Plague)
//!     .time(HistoricalTime::year(1347))
//!     .location(region_id)
//!     .participant(settlement_id)
//!     .effect(EventEffect::PopulationLoss { target: settlement_id, amount: 10000, duration_years: Some(50), cause: Some("The Great Plague".to_string()) })
//!     .build(world_id);
//! ```

